Subject: [PATCH 02431/11362] [outer-loop] RE + GameAdapter for tr87:
 glyph-substitution puzzle solved to L1

Operator: "pick one of the unsolved games and RE it" -> "register a GameAdapter
for tr87". tr87 was one of the 10 unsolved games (the fresh_env sweep showed it
is not blocked by non-idempotent reset -- it needs per-game RE).

MECHANIC (RE'd from frames + internal state, 2026-06-17): a CONFIG-SUBSTITUTION
puzzle. 5 editable glyphs (series B, value 1-7) must be set so each, via a visible
substitution rule (the top reference grid pairs A<->B values), matches the target
row (series A). Win = value(editable_i) == rule_map[value(target_i)] for all i.
ACTION1/2 cycle the selected glyph's value (+/-1 mod 7); ACTION3/4 move the
selector; move budget 128.

Two hypotheses were REFUTED before the right one: (a) direct 7bar-vs-Abar ink
match -- greedy plateaus at 42/64, never wins; (b) blind config-BFS -- exhausted
52k+ states / 120k nodes with no win. The win needs the SUBSTITUTION rule, so the
hand_verifier reads the rule map (cifzvbcuwqe) + target (zvojhrjxxm) + current
(ztgmtnnufb) -- the lp85 _goal_key internal-state pattern -- and returns the count
of positions not yet at their rule-mapped value (0 == win). That verifier routes
the best-first search to L1 in 94 STATES (vs 52k+ for blind BFS), reproduction-
gated reproduced=True (14 actions).

- GameAdapter _tr87 (action_labels/apply/full-grid state_key/rule-mapped verifier,
  branch_mode=replay) registered in _BUILDERS; solve_adaptered('tr87',1) ->
  offline_reproduced=True.
- 4 adapter unit tests (synthetic game, game-independent).
- metaharness RESOLVED via results/arc_loop_solve_tr87.json; aggregate now
  27 levels / 16 games (was 26/15).
- registry: full mechanic + dead-ends recorded (greedy-refuted, BFS-intractable,
  animation state_key, L2+ alter_rules twist) so the next attempt starts from here.

Frame-only perception (decoding glyph bitmaps + the rule grid from pixels) is a
future upgrade; the solve reproduces regardless (the gate replays actions).

